load ../credential-verify-endorse.maude

--- Delegation context throughout: operator > manager > clerk. stranger acts
--- for no one but itself. Identical to infoflow-integrity's fixtures, because
--- `verify` lowers to `endorse` on the SAME lattice -- that is the point.
---
--- Two families of search, deliberately kept apart:
---   RAISE-DEPENDENCY -- is verified(b2, R) producible at all? Each conjunct
---     of the raise gets its own No-solution when removed.
---   INJECTION -- does tainted data reach a control sink? The end-to-end
---     story on the shared lattice.
--- Conflating them would let "the raise did not happen" pass as "bad data did
--- not flow", which are different failures with different fixes.

--- Coverage: the raise happens when every conjunct holds -- matching
--- signature, governance grant, custodian custody, payload within the ceiling.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-VERIFY-ENDORSE :
  deleg((operator > manager) | (manager > clerk))
  inbound(b1, stranger) signedWith(b1, h1) granted(h1, operator) sealed(h1)
  bounded(b1, t1) verify(b1, b2, h1, t1)
  =>* C:Cfg verified(b2, operator) .

--- Coverage: the failure branch is reachable. A payload signed with a
--- different credential does not verify.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-VERIFY-ENDORSE :
  deleg((operator > manager) | (manager > clerk))
  inbound(b1, stranger) signedWith(b1, h2) granted(h1, operator) sealed(h1)
  bounded(b1, t1) verify(b1, b2, h1, t1)
  =>* C:Cfg verifyFailed(b2) .

--- Coverage, INJECTION: with no verify at all, inbound webhook content at an
--- operator-required control sink is an injection. This is the hazard the
--- crossing exists to close.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-VERIFY-ENDORSE :
  deleg((operator > manager) | (manager > clerk))
  inbound(b1, stranger) controlSink(b1, operator)
  =>* C:Cfg injection .

--- Coverage, INJECTION: verifying against a credential granted only clerk
--- authority does not license an operator-required sink. The raise happens,
--- but to an INSUFFICIENT authority -- the same partial-order direction
--- infoflow-integrity checks for endorse.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-VERIFY-ENDORSE :
  deleg((operator > manager) | (manager > clerk))
  inbound(b1, stranger) signedWith(b1, h1) granted(h1, clerk) sealed(h1)
  bounded(b1, t1) verify(b1, b2, h1, t1) controlSink(b2, operator)
  =>* C:Cfg injection .

--- Bite: FORGED SIGNATURE. The payload is signed with h2 but verified against
--- h1. Everything else is in place. No raise. This is the property that makes
--- the crossing cryptographic rather than asserted. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-VERIFY-ENDORSE :
  deleg((operator > manager) | (manager > clerk))
  inbound(b1, stranger) signedWith(b1, h2) granted(h1, operator) sealed(h1)
  bounded(b1, t1) verify(b1, b2, h1, t1)
  =>* verified(b2, operator) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: NO GOVERNANCE GRANT. The signature matches and the custodian holds
--- the key, but no grant names a vouching authority, so there is no authority
--- to vouch WITH. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-VERIFY-ENDORSE :
  deleg((operator > manager) | (manager > clerk))
  inbound(b1, stranger) signedWith(b1, h1) sealed(h1)
  bounded(b1, t1) verify(b1, b2, h1, t1)
  =>* verified(b2, operator) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: NOT CUSTODIAN-HELD. Governance grants the credential, but no
--- custodian holds it -- so the constant-time comparison never ran in the
--- principal that owns the key. This is where DR-0053's custody half and its
--- IFC half meet. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-VERIFY-ENDORSE :
  deleg((operator > manager) | (manager > clerk))
  inbound(b1, stranger) signedWith(b1, h1) granted(h1, operator)
  bounded(b1, t1) verify(b1, b2, h1, t1)
  =>* verified(b2, operator) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite: THE BANDWIDTH CEILING BINDS. The payload is bounded by t2 but the
--- statement declares `into t1`. I-IFC3 requires an integrity raise to carry a
--- mandatory bounded type; a mismatch raises nothing. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-VERIFY-ENDORSE :
  deleg((operator > manager) | (manager > clerk))
  inbound(b1, stranger) signedWith(b1, h1) granted(h1, operator) sealed(h1)
  bounded(b1, t2) verify(b1, b2, h1, t1)
  =>* verified(b2, operator) RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite, INJECTION: the whole point. A correctly verified payload drives an
--- operator-required control sink with no injection -- the inbound stranger
--- taint did NOT cross the raise. No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-VERIFY-ENDORSE :
  deleg((operator > manager) | (manager > clerk))
  inbound(b1, stranger) signedWith(b1, h1) granted(h1, operator) sealed(h1)
  bounded(b1, t1) verify(b1, b2, h1, t1) controlSink(b2, operator)
  =>* injection RESIDUAL:Cfg .

--- Bite, INJECTION: transitive acts-for still applies. A payload verified to
--- operator drives a manager-required sink safely, via operator > manager.
--- No solution.
search [1] in WHIPPLESCRIPT-CREDENTIAL-VERIFY-ENDORSE :
  deleg((operator > manager) | (manager > clerk))
  inbound(b1, stranger) signedWith(b1, h1) granted(h1, operator) sealed(h1)
  bounded(b1, t1) verify(b1, b2, h1, t1) controlSink(b2, manager)
  =>* injection RESIDUAL:Cfg .
